    {
      "data": {
        "text": "All the required files have been created successfully. The files are:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] start_oauth_login.py - starts an OAuth or OIDC authorization-code login\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] oauth_callback.py - handles the callback and exchanges an authorization code for tokens\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] profile_claims.py - fetches and normalizes federated user profile claims\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] pkce_login.py - implements a PKCE login flow for public clients\n5. [HELPER] identity_client.py - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Federated Login Flow\n6. [HELPER] identity_models.py - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Federated Login Flow\n7. [LATER-STEP] audit_summary.py - Summarizes federated-login audit events\n8. [LATER-STEP] claims_moderation.py - Moderates free-text claims or notes\n9. [LATER-STEP] consent_translate.py - Translates identity-provider consent copy\n10. [LATER-STEP] login_audit_store.py - Persists federated-login audit records in a managed document store\n\nEach scored implementation file uses a concrete external provider and makes that provider identifiable in code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
